  "summary": "Six preprints from 12–16 Nov establish tight or exact quantum bounds spanning query complexity, graph-state learning, and state-over-time cones.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is exact or matching characterization of quantum resources. Exact query algorithms are given for block compositions of Boolean functions, with rates tied to degree and adversary bounds. Tight bounded-error query bounds are proved for r-collision finding over bounded types, linking set-equality and k-distinctness regimes. A Haar-random oracle model of the python's lunch conjecture yields an Omega(2^{m/2}) decoding lower bound. Beyond query complexity, tight nonadaptive copy bounds and an adaptive separation are shown for learning graph states with local Pauli measurements. An exponential quantum memory advantage is shown for Dirichlet-energy testing under late-graph erasure. Convergent two-sided semidefinite hierarchies are given for the state-over-time cone. The new element is tightness and separations rather than only asymptotic gaps.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
